# Line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is the Git for Windows default, so every text file is
# checked out with CRLF. Harmless for the files that only ever run on the
# control PC -- but scripts/rp_fastread.py runs ON THE BOARD, which is Linux.
# A CRLF shebang makes `./rp_fastread.py` fail with the memorable and
# unhelpful "bad interpreter: python3^M".
#
# It is deployed and launched as `python3 /dev/shm/rp_fastread.py` today, and
# Python does not care about CRLF, so nothing is broken right now. This pins it
# so nothing breaks the day someone makes it executable instead.
* text=auto
scripts/rp_fastread.py text eol=lf
